entries.body:
DECIDED by human:purple, 2026-10-05. This implements finding ctx_77b1884dc8534f70.

- actionDigestFor gains an optional residualRef ("<epochId>#<index>"). It is omitted from the hash when absent, so existing digests do not change.
- planResidualSettlement, in the kernel, refuses unless all of these hold:
  - the stored epoch is FINALIZED and the index exists;
  - the reservation's residualRef matches;
  - the mandate is held by the transfer's FROM party;
  - the vault and chain equal the epoch's settlement domain;
  - the mandate is ACTIVE and unexpired, and the vault is not frozen;
  - validateExecutionBinding passes.
- The payee is the TO party's registered wallet on that chain, never the caller's. The settlement id is derived from (epochId, index), so it can be paid once.
- Before broadcasting, the API reads MitraClearing and refuses unless the epoch is Finalized or Settling and transfersOf(epoch)[index] equals the transfer being paid. The payment is then bound to the challengeable on-chain result.

Seams, built test-first:
(A) the kernel plan;
(B) POST /reservations with residualRef, whose terms must match the transfer;
(C) POST /settlements op settleResidual, paid once through the guard on a stub rail;
(D) a CLEARING_LIVE=1-gated live test that runs a whole epoch on-chain and pays the residuals through MitraVault v2.
